WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.501
-Thank you for being here, pal.
-My absolute pleasure.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.133
I miss you. I love you deeply.
-I do. I miss you.

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:06.267
I'm always happy to see you.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:11.167
We had a good
little exchange backstage.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:12.501
I think this could be
a new thing.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:13.767
-We did.
-Yeah.

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:17.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
I really -- I loved it.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:19.234
I love it
because it was so genuine.

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:20.567
It was real. It was real.

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:25.267
-Yeah, and surveys say
that it is 73% less bacteria.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:27.067
-That's exactly correct. Yeah.
-What did you call it?

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:28.467
A pinkie pound.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:29.701
-A pinkie point?

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:31.133
Oh, pinkie pound.
A pinkie pound, yeah.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:32.534
-A pinkie pound.
-Yeah, pinkie pound right there.

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:34.167
That's our thing.
I love it, yeah.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.267
I mean --
-It's big on TikTok.

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:36.467
-That's true.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:38.300
On TikTok, every kid is
doing pinkie pound.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.634
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:41.133
-Every time you're on the show,
we talk about music,

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:42.634
and I love to talk to you
about music,

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:43.868
because you're a great musician.

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:45.167
I know you love music.

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:48.100
How long have you been in your
band, 30 Seconds --

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.234
-Since -- I mean, forever.

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:52.534
My brother
and I started as kids.

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:56.334
And we actually signed
a record deal in 1998.

00:00:56.334 --> 00:00:57.701
And we've been doing it --
-'98.

00:00:57.701 --> 00:00:59.267
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
A long time.

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:02.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, thank you.

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:07.334
And, you know,
our last concert, in 2018,

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:09.801
was at Madison Square Garden
here in New York.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:10.868
-Was that right?
-Yeah.

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:13.267
And -- Of course.

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.467
But New York --
the best audiences in the world.

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:17.033
-No, it's unbelievable.
Yeah, and let's --

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:18.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
I mean, isn't that great?

00:01:18.968 --> 00:01:20.334
I agree, but do you --

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:22.968
-My point was, it's just amazing
to do it this long,

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:26.634
and our last show was arguably
one of our best shows,

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:29.367
and it was at, you know, the
most iconic venue in the world.

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:33.267
-MSG. Do you ever -- Do you
pinch yourself when you play?

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:35.634
-Often.

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:38.667
-I mean...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:40.634
-Oh, like you don't.
-No, yeah --

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:41.868
-Like you don't.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:44.434
-Someone's like,
"I'd pinch you, Jared."

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:47.400
No, I mean, like when
you think of your upbringing.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:50.033
And you're a kid.
You didn't have much.

00:01:50.033 --> 00:01:51.767
You didn't have
any musical instruments.

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:52.767
-Yeah.
-You borrowed a guitar, right?

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:53.934
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:57.167
No, we were pretty --
You know, my mom --

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:59.701
We were born in Louisiana.

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:01.467
-Yeah.
-We didn't have a lot.

00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:05.133
My mom put herself through
college, went back to school.

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:07.334
She had dropped out of high
school and went back to school

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:09.934
and then went to nursing school
and, you know,

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:12.734
wanted to make a better life
for herself and her kids.

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:14.734
And she taught us a lot,
you know?

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.067
I owe her a lot.
-Yeah.

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:18.534
-She really taught us that
the impossible is possible

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:19.667
if you're willing
to do the hard work.

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:20.801
-Yeah. And you do --

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:22.567
-I mean, you're going to
make me cry up here.

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:25.000
-Yeah, that's not my --
You do the hard work.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.901
That's good.
-Yeah.

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:28.200
-You do do the hard work.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.501
I mean, from every role
that you've been on,

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:32.868
you've been nice enough
to come on our show.

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:35.300
You've either lost 40 pounds.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.634
You gained 60 pounds.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:39.534
Like, you do this stuff,
extreme stuff.

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:41.734
You put the work in,
and it pays off.

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:42.868
I mean, here you are.

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:43.901
You're selling out
Madison Square Garden,

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:44.934
for God's sakes.

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:46.434
-Yeah, it's incredible.

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:48.601
And, you know, the older I get,
I just have an

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:51.634
enormous sense of gratitude
to do what I do.

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:54.901
And, you know,
the transformative process,

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:56.434
for me,
is really fascinating.

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:57.934
I love immersive acting.

00:02:57.934 --> 00:03:01.000
I love to see if I can
really create a new life

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.634
and share it with people.

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:04.501
And that's what I did in
"House of Gucci"

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:06.534
with the one-and-only
Paolo Gucci.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:07.801
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:07.801 --> 00:03:09.000
-Paolo Gucci.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.400
I mean, you're unrecognizable
in this film.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.400
But, also, the way you --

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.267
Your accent is unbelievable,
as well.

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:20.534
It's -- Well, here's the thing.

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:22.701
When I see you,
I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.801
I just -- I talk to you.
We have fun. We laugh.

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:25.901
And then I see you
in front of --

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:27.267
What was the one concert?

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:29.334
I think it was like 100,000
people or something crazy.

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:30.901
-Yeah, it's -- You know,

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:33.267
we spent a lot of time
on the road touring.

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:36.067
So, as you guys know,
our life is really

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:37.868
about being on the road.

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:39.834
Every song that we write --
We actually --

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:41.334
In COVID, I wrote over --

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:44.868
I think it's
about 264 songs now.

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:46.567
It's amazing what a little --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:48.033
Thank you very much, yeah.

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:49.934
You haven't heard them yet,
so hold the applause.

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:53.100
-Yeah. 263 are eh,
but one is whoo!

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.434
-It's amazing what a little --

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:58.234
A little banana bread
really stokes the creativity.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:03:59.801
Like, I shut down
a banana bread.

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:01.434
-A little banana bread.
-A little "Tiger King."

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:02.534
Bam!
-It goes a long way.

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:03.934
-Exactly. It goes a long way.

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:06.000
-But I'm actually having
a hard time

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.667
coming up with an album title.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:11.367
And I thought, you're a such --
He's so great with music.

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:14.000
I mean, the voice of
an angel you have.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.100
Really do.
-Thank you so much.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.367
-You do.
-I mean, yeah.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:17.667
-But I thought maybe you could
help me come up --

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.000
-Yes. Yes.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.634
-And if you have a good one,
I'm going to take it,

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:21.667
just so you know.

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:23.334
-You are?
-Yes. Absolutely.

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:26.133
-Alright, so, this is
all these songs you wrote.

00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:27.534
All 264.

00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:29.300
-Yeah, it was a dark --
It's a tough time.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.934
I thought maybe one could be,
you know, something edgy

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.767
like [bleep] you,
you [bleep] [bleep]

00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:35.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.901 --> 00:04:40.234
It's a little angry, I know.
-Yeah. I already had that.

00:04:40.234 --> 00:04:43.200
-Or maybe
"The Incredible True Adventures

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.167
of a Labradoodle Named..."

00:04:46.167 --> 00:04:48.334
-Uh, Tortney.

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:50.000
-Tortney!

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.868
-How about the --
-Tortney.

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:55.534
-Exiting a cave.

00:04:55.534 --> 00:04:57.033
-Exiting a cave?
-The exit -- Yeah.

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:59.701
Oh, how about --
-Yeah.

00:04:59.701 --> 00:05:01.701
-Tomago.
-Tomago.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:05.334
-How about --
how about "Egg Life"?

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:08.100
-We could do -- We could name
it after someone --

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.434
-You guys are all in
an egg, like that.

00:05:09.434 --> 00:05:11.334
-Yeah, we're in egg heads.

00:05:11.334 --> 00:05:13.601
-Yeah, you got egg heads.
-It's like a Bowie thing.

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:15.033
-Yeah, you don't --
You're not quite --

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:16.667
It's called
"Not Ready to Hatch."

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:21.734
-We could name it after someone
who has done something,

00:05:21.734 --> 00:05:23.100
you know, remarkable.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.167
Like, we'd name it after a
real person, like Elon Musk

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:27.734
or maybe Kanye.

00:05:27.734 --> 00:05:29.801
He's not using his name anymore.

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:32.133
-No, yeah.
He got rid of his name.

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:34.467
Yeah, legally,
we're allowed to get --

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.701
"Kanye" is the name of the next
30 Seconds to Mars album.

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:38.000
-Thank you very much.
-That's it right there.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.767
"Kanye."
-Thank you.

00:05:39.767 --> 00:05:41.033
-He's not using it.
-Thank you!

00:05:41.033 --> 00:05:42.033
-You got it.

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:43.267
-Thank you!
-You should do that.

00:05:43.267 --> 00:05:44.801
-I appreciate it.

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:46.234
-Can I just ask you about
a couple photos?

00:05:46.234 --> 00:05:47.934
Because I love
showing pictures of you,

00:05:47.934 --> 00:05:51.801
because I live vicariously
through you in these photos.

00:05:51.801 --> 00:05:54.100
I knew you're very into
rock-climbing.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:55.234
-Yes. Yes.

00:05:55.234 --> 00:05:56.767
-Or do you just call it
climbing?

00:05:56.767 --> 00:05:58.067
Is there a name for it?

00:05:58.067 --> 00:06:00.367
-We call it rock-climbing.

00:06:00.367 --> 00:06:01.467
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:01.467 --> 00:06:04.467
-Wow. Here's a picture.
This is real.

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:05.467
I didn't --

00:06:05.467 --> 00:06:07.567
-Yeah.
-Yeah. No filter here.

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:10.501
-Yeah.
-That's Jared Leto. Yeah.

00:06:10.501 --> 00:06:13.934
And are you on a cord?
Or what's happening? No.

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:15.501
-We call it a rope.

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:16.501
-You were on a rope.

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:17.734
-We call it a rope.

00:06:17.734 --> 00:06:19.968
But this is actually more --

00:06:19.968 --> 00:06:22.501
It kind of has
a bouldering vibe to it.

00:06:22.501 --> 00:06:24.100
Bouldering is when
you don't use a rope,

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:27.067
but you climb,
you know, boulders.

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:28.334
-Yeah, that's bouldering.

00:06:28.334 --> 00:06:30.501
-Yeah, I love it.
It's a passion of mine.

00:06:30.501 --> 00:06:32.801
And, yeah,
that was recently in Sardinia.

00:06:32.801 --> 00:06:34.501
I was actually with
my good friend,

00:06:34.501 --> 00:06:36.033
Alex Honnold, from "Free Solo."

00:06:36.033 --> 00:06:38.267
-Oh, "Free Solo." Of course.
That guy's a legend.

00:06:38.267 --> 00:06:39.667
-He's right down here.

00:06:39.667 --> 00:06:40.868
-I mean, look at that.
That's insane.

00:06:40.868 --> 00:06:44.834
Do you get frightened
or did you get --

00:06:44.834 --> 00:06:46.100
-No, no, no, no.

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:47.434
I mean, you could wear
a diaper, I guess,

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:48.501
if you're worried
about it, but --

00:06:48.501 --> 00:06:49.834
-I would.

00:06:49.834 --> 00:06:53.200
-But I'm pretty used to it now
and I absolutely love it.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.067
You seem like
you would be great at it,

00:06:55.067 --> 00:06:57.901
because I've always gotten the
sense that you're very limber.

00:06:57.901 --> 00:06:59.200
-Oh.

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:02.934
Do you get that sense?
-Do you not get that sense?

00:07:02.934 --> 00:07:04.067
-You get that sense from me?

00:07:04.067 --> 00:07:05.667
-I thought that
you were very flexible.

00:07:05.667 --> 00:07:07.734
-Well, no, I'm just
all upper-body strength.

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:10.067
-Oh, you are?
-My legs are very weak.

00:07:10.067 --> 00:07:11.167
-Oh, yeah. Well, me too.

00:07:11.167 --> 00:07:12.367
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:07:12.367 --> 00:07:14.000
-I mean, here, do you want --
Just lift me.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.000
-No, no, no, no.
I'd probably drop you.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.200
I'm, you know --

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:20.167
-I just -- That's the only way
I can kind of

00:07:20.167 --> 00:07:21.367
get out of chairs now.

00:07:21.367 --> 00:07:23.801
I've spent all
my time upper body

00:07:23.801 --> 00:07:26.400
that I have forgotten
about my legs.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:29.734
And I could stand right here,
but just very weak.

00:07:29.734 --> 00:07:32.067
-That's pretty good.
Pretty good. Pretty good.

00:07:32.067 --> 00:07:34.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:34.467 --> 00:07:36.634
But I would love to
take you sometime,

00:07:36.634 --> 00:07:38.834
if you'd like to go with
me, Alex Honnold.

00:07:38.834 --> 00:07:39.901
-I would love to go.

00:07:39.901 --> 00:07:41.133
Would I bother you?

00:07:41.133 --> 00:07:42.200
I wouldn't want to bother you
and ruin the --

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.033
-You probably would.
-I would, yeah.

00:07:44.033 --> 00:07:45.400
I don't want to ruin
the experience for you.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.400
Like, you're up here because
you don't want to see me.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.801
-No, no, no, no.

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:51.100
-You're going to the top of
a place where there's no humans.

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:53.234
You're like, "I'm good, man.
I want to get up here."

00:07:53.234 --> 00:07:54.467
So you don't want to be
with Jimmy Fallon

00:07:54.467 --> 00:07:56.167
going like,
"Hey, man, can you show me --"

00:07:56.167 --> 00:07:57.501
-You could do part of a show

00:07:57.501 --> 00:07:59.501
hanging from the side of
the cliff in Yosemite.

00:07:59.501 --> 00:08:01.934
El Captain.
Wouldn't that be amazing?

00:08:01.934 --> 00:08:03.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:06.467 --> 00:08:07.601
-Can we --

00:08:07.601 --> 00:08:09.634
-Alex could probably
put you on his shoulders

00:08:09.634 --> 00:08:11.267
and carry you up there.

00:08:11.267 --> 00:08:13.000
-Alex -- I would do that.
Yeah, if you want.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.767
I weigh like,
well, you know, about 120.

00:08:14.767 --> 00:08:15.901
-Yeah.

00:08:15.901 --> 00:08:17.868
-Yeah, 120 pounds,
something like that.

00:08:17.868 --> 00:08:19.234
Yeah, so I can just
hop on his back.

00:08:19.234 --> 00:08:21.200
What do you carry
in your backpack?

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.267
Carabiners?
-Excuse me?

00:08:23.267 --> 00:08:26.000
-Carabiners.
-Oh, I thought you said wieners.

00:08:27.267 --> 00:08:28.267
-A can of wieners.

00:08:28.267 --> 00:08:29.334
-I was like, "Actually..."
No.

00:08:29.334 --> 00:08:30.501
-A can of wieners? Yeah.

00:08:30.501 --> 00:08:33.234
Yeah, a can of wiener.
Vienna sausage is --

00:08:33.234 --> 00:08:35.734
-Carabiner, can of wieners --
that's something.

00:08:35.734 --> 00:08:37.167
-Something there.
-We should go on "Shark Tank."

00:08:37.167 --> 00:08:38.934
-Album title!
-Oh, album title!

00:08:38.934 --> 00:08:42.000
-Hey!
-"Can of Wieners"!

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.834
Jared, I want to
talk to you about --

00:08:43.834 --> 00:08:45.267
I want to talk to you about
"House of Gucci," okay?

00:08:45.267 --> 00:08:46.334
More with Jared Leto
when we come back.

00:08:46.334 --> 00:08:47.467
Come on back, everybody.

